    <briefdescription>
<para>Integration tests for <computeroutput><ref refid="" kindref="compound">XtcProjectCreator</ref></computeroutput> that verify generated projects are valid Gradle projects that can be configured successfully. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>These tests create actual projects and run <javadoccode>./gradlew tasks</javadoccode> to verify the build files are syntactically correct and the project structure is valid.</para>
<para><bold>DISABLED BY DEFAULT</bold>: These tests spawn separate Gradle processes for each generated project, which downloads dependencies, the Gradle wrapper, and configures the project from scratch. With an empty cache, this adds several minutes to the build.</para>
<para>Requirements: <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>The XTC plugin must be available in mavenLocal() - run <javadoccode>./gradlew publishLocal</javadoccode> first </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Network access for Gradle wrapper download (first run only) </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Enable these tests by setting environment variable: <javadoccode>RUN_INTEGRATION_TESTS=true</javadoccode></para>
<para>// TODO: Consider running these tests in CI on a scheduled basis (nightly) rather than on every build // TODO: Consider using TestKit with a shared Gradle home to speed up repeated runs // TODO: Consider caching the Gradle wrapper and dependencies in CI </para>
    </detaileddescription>
